WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Deposit 1,000 dollars
in a checking account,

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.440
and your bank doesn't lock it all away.

3
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.880
Banks keep only a fraction
of deposits as reserves.

4
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.300
In fact, since March 2020,

5
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.280
the Fed's required reserve
ratio has been 0 percent.

6
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.030
Yet banks still make new
loans every single day.

7
00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.870
So when a bank lends you money,

8
00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:23.520
whose money are you actually borrowing?

9
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.560
In this mission, you'll
read a bank's T-account:

10
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.210
required reserves, excess
reserves and loans.

11
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.720
Then you'll change the
reserve ratio in a graph

12
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.910
lab and watch deposits grow,

13
00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:36.620
round by round.

14
00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.440
Your mission: track where the
money in a loan really comes from.
